        "\n",
        "### Cryptographic Background: HMAC-SHA256\n",
        "\n",
        "**HMAC (Hash-based Message Authentication Code)** is a cryptographic\n",
        "construction that uses a secret key and a message to produce an\n",
        "authentication tag.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this experiment, we use HMAC-SHA256 as an educational substitute\n",
        "for the historical GSM A3 authentication algorithm.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Inputs:**\n",
        "- Secret key (Ki): 128 bits in our experiment\n",
        "- Random challenge (RAND): 128 bits\n",
        "\n",
        "**Output:**\n",
        "- HMAC-SHA256: 256 bits\n",
        "- Demo SRES: First 32 bits of the HMAC output\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Security properties:**\n",
        "- The same key and message produce the same output.\n",
        "- Changing the key or message generally changes the output.\n",
        "- Without the secret key, generating a valid tag for a new message\n",
        "  should be computationally infeasible.\n",
        "- HMAC provides message authentication and integrity, not encryption.\n",
        "\n",
        " **Security Properties**\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Integrity:** Detects unauthorized changes to the message.\n",
        "- **Authentication:** Verifies that the sender knows the secret key.\n",
        "- **Confidentiality:** NOT provided. The message remains readable.\n",
        "- **Replay protection:** NOT provided by HMAC alone.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Applications:** API authentication, webhook verification,\n",
        "message integrity, and certain TLS constructions.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Connection to GSM:**\n",
        "\n",
        "In our educational simulation:\n",
        "\n",
        "    SRES = HMAC-SHA256(Ki, RAND)[:4]\n",
        "\n",
        "This produces a 32-bit response, matching the size of GSM SRES.\n",
        "\n",
        "Note: Real historical GSM A3 implementations, such as COMP128,\n",
        "do not use this HMAC-SHA256 construction.\n"
      ]
    },
