        "\n",
        "## Part 5 — GSM A5: Radio Encryption and Decryption\n",
        "\n",
        "### Learning Objectives\n",
        "\n",
        "After this experiment, students should be able to:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Explain the purpose of the GSM A5 cipher family.\n",
        "- Understand the relationship between A8 and A5.\n",
        "- Explain how a keystream is used to encrypt data.\n",
        "- Understand why the sender and receiver need the same\n",
        "  session key and synchronized frame information.\n",
        "- Explain why different frame inputs produce different\n",
        "  keystreams.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Background\n",
        "\n",
        "In the previous experiment, A8 generated a 64-bit\n",
        "session key called Kc.\n",
        "\n",
        "GSM uses the A5 family of algorithms to protect\n",
        "communication over the radio interface.\n",
        "\n",
        "A5 stream ciphers generate a keystream using the\n",
        "session key Kc and frame-dependent information.\n",
        "\n",
        "The keystream is combined with the plaintext using\n",
        "the XOR operation.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Encryption:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Ciphertext = Plaintext XOR Keystream\n",
        "\n",
        "**Decryption:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Plaintext = Ciphertext XOR Keystream\n",
        "\n",
        "This works because:\n",
        "\n",
        "(A XOR B) XOR B = A\n",
        "\n",
        "### Experiment\n",
        "\n",
        "We investigate three scenarios:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Correct encryption and decryption:** Both sides use\n",
        "   the same Kc and frame number.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **New frame number:** The same plaintext produces\n",
        "   different ciphertext.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Incorrect frame number:** The receiver generates\n",
        "   the wrong keystream and cannot recover the message.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Important Technical Note\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook uses HMAC-SHA256 to generate a demonstration\n",
        "keystream.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is NOT a real implementation of GSM A5/1, A5/2, or A5/3.\n",
        "\n",
        "Real GSM encryption operates on radio-frame data with\n",
        "protocol-specific inputs and processing. This example\n",
        "uses a short text message only to demonstrate the\n",
        "principle of stream encryption.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Discussion Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Why do the sender and receiver need the same Kc?\n",
        "2. Why does changing the frame number change ciphertext?\n",
        "3. What happens if the receiver uses the wrong frame number?\n",
        "4. Does A5 protect communication beyond the radio interface?\n"
      ]
    },
