        "\n",
        "## Attack Lab — Keystream Reuse in Stream Ciphers\n",
        "\n",
        "### Learning Objectives\n",
        "\n",
        "After this experiment, students should be able to:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Explain why reusing a stream-cipher keystream is dangerous.\n",
        "- Understand how an attacker can exploit known plaintext.\n",
        "- Recover a second plaintext without knowing the secret key.\n",
        "- Explain why different keystreams are important.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Background\n",
        "\n",
        "A stream cipher encrypts plaintext using XOR:\n",
        "\n",
        "C = P XOR K\n",
        "\n",
        "where:\n",
        "- P = Plaintext\n",
        "- C = Ciphertext\n",
        "- K = Keystream\n",
        "\n",
        "If two messages use the same keystream:\n",
        "\n",
        "C1 = P1 XOR K\n",
        "C2 = P2 XOR K\n",
        "\n",
        "An attacker who knows P1 and intercepts C1 can recover K:\n",
        "\n",
        "K = P1 XOR C1\n",
        "\n",
        "The attacker can then recover the second message:\n",
        "\n",
        "P2 = C2 XOR K\n",
        "\n",
        "The attacker does not need to know the session key Kc.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Attack Scenario\n",
        "\n",
        "We compare two situations:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scenario 1 — Keystream Reuse**\n",
        "- Two messages are encrypted with the same Kc and frame input.\n",
        "- The attacker knows the first plaintext.\n",
        "- The attacker intercepts both ciphertexts.\n",
        "- The second plaintext can be recovered.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scenario 2 — Different Frame Input**\n",
        "- The second message uses a different frame input.\n",
        "- The demo generates a different keystream.\n",
        "- The previously recovered keystream no longer decrypts it.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Important Note\n",
        "\n",
        "This is an intentional misuse of our educational\n",
        "HMAC-based A5 substitute.\n",
        "\n",
        "It demonstrates a general stream-cipher vulnerability,\n",
        "not a verified attack against a real GSM deployment.\n",
        "\n",
        "Changing the frame input helps avoid this specific reuse\n",
        "only when the resulting keystream is different.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Discussion Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Why does the attacker not need to know Kc?\n",
        "2. What information must the attacker possess?\n",
        "3. What happens if both plaintexts are unknown?\n",
        "4. Why is reusing a keystream dangerous?\n"
      ]
    },
